@title Borrowing FAQ
@subtitle Millbrook Public Library. No more late fines from 2026-11-01.
@author Hye-jin Park, Circulation Manager
@date 2026-11-01

! **Good news:** from 2026-11-01 we no longer charge late fines.

## Who can join the library?

Anyone who lives, works or studies in Millbrook County can join. Membership is free.

Children under 18 need a parent or guardian to sign them up.

## How many items can I borrow?

You can borrow up to 30 items at once. Within that:

- Up to 5 can be DVDs.
- Up to 2 can be Wi-Fi hotspots.

## How long can I keep things?

table = Item,Loan period; Books,21 days; Audiobooks,21 days; DVDs,7 days; Wi-Fi hotspots,14 days

## What if I return something late?

There are no late fines from 2026-11-01. Just bring it back when you can.

But please don't keep things too long:

- After 30 days overdue, we treat the item as lost and charge its replacement cost. The most we charge is $25 per item.
- If your account owes $10 or more, borrowing is paused until it is paid.

!! An item 30 days overdue counts as lost, and you are charged up to $25 for it.

## How do I renew?

You can renew online, in the app or at the desk. You can renew an item up to 3 times, unless another reader is waiting for it.

## How do I reserve an item?

Reservations are free. You can have up to 15 at once.

When your item is ready, we email you. It waits for you at the desk for 7 days.

---

**Still have a question?** Email [help@millbrooklibrary.example](mailto:help@millbrooklibrary.example) or visit the desk on weekdays from 09:00 to 18:00.
